Merge an import line at the front of a user sheet

A user sheet of another toolkit drops an import that stands after a
rule. The line of the writer must therefore stand first in such a
file. The GTK files take the line at the end, and those bytes must
not move.

The merge now takes a placement value. The end arm keeps the append
to the trimmed content. The front arm puts the line after a leading
@charset rule and before every other byte. A parser reads that rule
at the head of a file alone. The front arm copies every other byte
in place, so a file of another line ending keeps it.

The front arm cuts at the semicolon of the charset rule, not at the
first line break. A sheet that holds the rule and a style rule on
one line therefore takes the import before that style rule. The
remove pass takes back the bytes of the front merge alone, so such
a sheet gives its exact bytes back.

The import line follows the lock names into the main file of the
binary, so each writer owns the line that it merges.

The change sits on the branch work/firefox-theme of the local tree, as
commit 3 of 10. The branch holds those ten commits above the head of
work/gtk4-theme, which merge request !15 on system/qtcurve holds. The fork
wyn/qtcurve holds work/firefox-theme. Merge request !29 on system/qtcurve
holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

